.TH IMUD\-INFLUXDB 8 "July 2026" "imud 1.1" "System Manager's Manual"
.SH NAME
imud\-influxdb \- bridge imud's binary stream to InfluxDB line protocol
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B imud-influxdb
[\fB\-\-config\fR \fIPATH\fR]
[\fB\-\-version\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B imud-influxdb
connects to the local AF_UNIX binary subscription stream published by
.BR imud (8)
and writes one InfluxDB
.I line-protocol
point per tick, for time-series storage and Grafana dashboards (fusion tuning,
sea-trial logging).  Two transports are supported:
.TP
.B udp
Fire-and-forget datagrams to InfluxDB 1.x's UDP listener or Telegraf's
.I socket_listener
(the usual path into InfluxDB 2.x/3.x).  Configure the listener precision as ns.
.TP
.B http
A plaintext HTTP POST per point to
.I /write
(1.x) or
.I /api/v2/write
(2.x), with an optional
.B Authorization: Token
header.  No TLS \(em front a cloud/TLS endpoint with a local proxy.
.PP
The bridge holds no hardware and is pure C (no external dependencies).  It reads
the stream socket named by its own
.B socket
key (default
.IR /run/imud/imud-stream.sock ),
so
.BR imud (8)
must have its
.B [stream]
output enabled, and it reconnects automatically if imud restarts.
.PP
Each point carries the measurement (default
.IR imud ),
a
.B source
tag, and fields: quaternion
.RB ( qw , qx , qy , qz ),
.BR roll / pitch / yaw ,
.BR heading ,
.BR heading_true / variation
(when declination is known),
.BR rate_of_turn ,
.B heave
(when
.B publish_heave
is set),
.BR temp ,
and an integer
.BR seq ,
timestamped with the packet's wall-clock time in nanoseconds.  Angles are degrees
.RB ( units " = " deg )
or radians
.RB ( units " = " rad ).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-config \ PATH
Load configuration from
.I PATH
instead of
.IR /etc/imud/imud-influxdb.conf .
Only the
.B [imud-influxdb]
section is read.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version string and exit.
.SH SIGNALS
.TP
.B SIGHUP
Reload the configuration.  The rate, measurement, source tag, units, heave
inclusion, UDP destination, and log level are applied live; the transport and
HTTP target require a restart.  If the reload fails to parse, the running
configuration is kept.
.TP
.BR SIGTERM ", " SIGINT
Graceful shutdown.
.SH CONFIGURATION
The bridge reads its own file (default
.IR /etc/imud/imud-influxdb.conf ),
using only the
.B [imud-influxdb]
section.  Key groups:
.TP
.BR enabled ", " socket ", " transport
Start the bridge; imud stream socket to read;
.BR udp | http .
[restart]
.TP
.BR rate_hz ", " measurement ", " source_label ", " units ", " publish_heave
Emit rate, measurement name, value of the
.B source
tag, units
.RB ( deg | rad ),
and whether to include heave.  [hot]
.TP
.BR udp_addr ", " udp_port
UDP destination (default 127.0.0.1:8089).  [hot]
.TP
.BR http_host ", " http_port ", " http_path ", " http_token
HTTP host/port (default 127.0.0.1:8086), write path (with the db or
org/bucket and precision query), and an optional InfluxDB 2.x API token (stored
in plaintext \(em protect the file).  [restart]
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/imud/imud-influxdb.conf
Default configuration file.
.SH EXAMPLES
Run against a local InfluxDB 1.x UDP listener:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
imud-influxdb --config /etc/imud/imud-influxdb.conf
.EE
.RE
.PP
Enable as a service (after enabling imud's
.B [stream]
output and
.B enabled
in
.IR imud-influxdb.conf ):
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
sudo systemctl enable --now imud-influxdb
.EE
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR imud (8),
.BR imud-signalk (8),
.BR imud-mqtt (8),
.BR imud.conf (5)
